WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.000
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.501
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:07.934
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.267
And, guys,
this is very exciting.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.167
Legendary actor Al Pacino
is my guest tonight!

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.100
-Come on.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.234
-All I know is,
if Al Pacino were in Congress,

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.300
we would have had a
speaker of the House on day one.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.434
[ As Pacino ] Vote for McCarthy

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:27.267
and say hello to
my little friend!

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.868
[ Normal voice ] That's right.
Everyone's talking about this.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.901
Earlier Saturday morning,
after four days

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.834
and 15 rounds of voting,
Kevin McCarthy

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:35.601
was sworn in as
speaker of the House.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.767
McCarthy was like,

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.634
"I'm just glad
it didn't go to a 16th vote.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:41.667
That would have been
humiliating."

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.601
I can't even imagine what
McCarthy was going through.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.734
It must have felt like
sitting outside Applebee's

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:49.234
and waiting four days for
your disk to buzz.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.901
"I'm in! I'm in! I'm in!"

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.434
After 15 rounds of voting,

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.534
McCarthy pulled off
the impossible --

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:59.300
he got people to watch C-SPAN
for an entire week.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.133
Speaking of C-SPAN, you can tell
even they were annoyed

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.601
with how long the voting took.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.734
Just check out what
they did after the announcement.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:08.734
-The honorable Kevin McCarthy
of the state of California

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.634
is duly elected speaker
of the House of Representatives.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:12.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:13.934
-♪ It's about damn time ♪

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:16.267
♪♪

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:18.033
-Come on.
-Wow.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.601
-That was just
a little unprofessional.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.167
Some more big news
from Washington.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.000
I read that President Biden's
all in for 2024

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.434
and is preparing to launch
his re-election campaign

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:30.501
in February.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.834
That's smart.

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:35.868
See how Valentine's Day goes,
then make it official.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.934
Meanwhile, this weekend,
Biden traveled to Texas

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.167
and visited the southern border
for the first time

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.634
since taking office.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.834
After walking around
for a few hours, Biden said,

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.067
"Well, just as I thought.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:48.300
Being here
did absolutely nothing."

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.667
At one point, a few migrants
saw Biden at the border

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:54.567
and were like, "Good Lord,
how long is the wait to get in?"

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:58.000
Well, people...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.868
People were talking about
this last night.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.667
Prince Harry sat down for
a "60 Minutes" interview

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.100
with Anderson Cooper.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.868
Yeah, Prince Harry
and Anderson Cooper.

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:09.567
The theme was "Fire and Ice."

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.234
But the "60 Minutes" interview
was a great chance

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.033
to hear Harry and Meghan's story

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.234
in case you missed their
two-hour sit-down with Oprah

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:23.100
or their
six-part Netflix documentary.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.534
We really want to hear what
you -- Yeah.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.934
Hey, guys, I saw that
the Mega Millions jackpot

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.434
has jumped to more than
$1 billion.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:31.567
[ Record scratch ]

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:34.033
-Say what?!

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:43.300
-Yep, the jackpot is now worth
an estimated $1.1 billion,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.667
with $568 million in cash.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:49.200
-Say what?!

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.934
-If someone wins, it would be
the third-largest amount

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.334
in Mega Millions history.

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:57.501
-Say what?!

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.367
-That's right. And get this.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.701
If no one wins tomorrow,

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.567
the jackpot will be
even higher on Friday!

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.400
-Enough, Jimmy! Enough!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.834
[ Explosion,
funk music playing ]

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:18.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.801
-Some business news.

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:27.534
I saw that M&amp;M'S is celebrating
women by releasing packages

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:30.300
that only contain
the three female candies.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.367
[ Crowd cheering ]
I know what you're thinking.

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.868
"Can't the packaging just say,
'No Nuts'?"

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.734
-Hey!

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:40.067
Say what?!

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.801
-And, finally, TSA agents
at an airport in Florida

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:48.601
found a 4-foot emotional-support
boa constrictor

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.467
in a woman's carry-on bag.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.467
Seriously, how stressed
do you have to be

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:56.767
for a boa constrictor
to calm you down?

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.501
Ladies and gentlemen,
we have a great show tonight.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:00.601
Guys, do you ever see
a photo in the news

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.868
and you think that headline
should be different?

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.033
We're gonna take care of that
right now.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.734
It's time for
"News and Improved."

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.067
Here we go.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:13.100
-♪ News and Improved ♪

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.534
-For example,
check out this first photo.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:20.934
The original headline was...

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.734
That headline
can definitely be improved

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.534
because if you only looked
at the photo,

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:28.467
the headline could have been...

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:29.968
It's like...

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.634
[ Applause ]

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:39.901
Up next, this headline says...

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:44.868
But the headline
could have been...

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.000
[ Applause ]

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.334
-"What?!"

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:54.434
-The next headline was...

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:59.067
The headline could have been...

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:02.033
[ Applause ]

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:09.234
Next headline was...

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:13.968
